<BlogPost
  title="LED Prep in Shiloh and Eclipse: Internal, External, and Continuous Pull — Complete Spec Guide"
  description="Every way to prep Shiloh and Eclipse cabinets for LED lighting: internal panel routes ($100 list per panel), Cabinet Lighting Channel for wall, floating shelf, and toe kick, and the continuous-pull option for handleless walls. Route positions, caveats, and what the dealer supplies."
  author="Ben Miller"
  publishedDate="2026-09-04"
  ogImage="/images/blog/led-prep-shiloh-eclipse/listing-card.webp"
  heroImage="/images/blog/led-prep-shiloh-eclipse/internal-led-channel-positions.webp"
>

<p>Lighting is one of the easiest ways to make a design stand apart, and clients increasingly expect it — for visibility at the counter and for ambiance after dark. Shiloh and Eclipse can be prepped at the factory for <strong>external</strong> lighting (under wall cabinets, under floating shelves, at the toe kick), for <strong>internal</strong> lighting (inside the cabinet, on the side or top panels), and for a <strong>continuous pull</strong> that lights a handleless wall. Internal LED prep, released in June, is taking off. Here's the full picture in one place.</p>

<p><strong>One rule applies to every option below: the LED tape itself is not supplied.</strong> W.W. Wood routes the cabinet and supplies the channel; the dealer sources the LED lighting locally.</p>

<h2>1. Internal LED prep — light the inside of the cabinet</h2>

<p>LED prep can be ordered on the <strong>interior panels</strong> of a cabinet. W.W. Wood routes a channel into the panel; you order <strong>CLC (Cabinet Lighting Channel)</strong> to sit in the route and house your locally sourced LED tape.</p>

<h3>Why designers use it</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Illuminate the entire interior of a cabinet</li>
  <li>Showcase art and decorative glassware in glass-door uppers</li>
  <li>Highlight two-tone interiors</li>
</ul>

<h3>Pricing</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>$100 list per panel routed.</strong> Apply one modification per panel.</li>
  <li>Example: vertical prep on both the left and right side panels = 2 × $100 = <strong>$200 list</strong>.</li>
  <li>Order enough CLC to field-trim and insert into the route at installation.</li>
</ul>

<h3>How to specify it</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Choose the direction of the route: <strong>Vertical</strong> (on the side panels) or <strong>Horizontal</strong> (on the top panel).</li>
  <li>Choose the offset: <strong>Front, Middle, or Back</strong> (positions below).</li>
  <li>Apply one $100 list modification per panel.</li>
  <li>Add CLC to the order to field-trim and install.</li>
</ol>

