<h3>Caveats — read before you quote</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Horizontal routes are not available in corner cabinets.</strong></li>
  <li><strong>Each routed panel is $100 list.</strong> Left and right vertical prep on one cabinet is $200.</li>
  <li><strong>Stacked wall cabinets with vertical prep</strong> get the route through <strong>both the top and bottom sections</strong>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. External LED prep — Cabinet Lighting Channel</h2>

<p>For light <em>below</em> the cabinetry, W.W. Wood grooves the cabinet for a field-installed <strong>CLC Cabinet Lighting Channel</strong>. There are three applications:</p>

<div class="post-figure">
  <img src="/images/blog/led-prep-shiloh-eclipse/cabinet-lighting-channel-applications.webp" alt="W.W. Wood Cabinet Lighting Channel spec page with section drawings for floating shelf, wall cabinet, and toe kick applications" width="1545" height="1999" loading="lazy" />
</div>

<h3>Wall cabinets</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Order the <strong>Prep Wall For Lighting</strong> modification (spec book page C2).</li>
  <li>The cabinet bottom shelf is grooved for the CLC channel, and the <strong>cabinet sides get a pre-grooved wire chase</strong>.</li>
  <li>Wall cabinet sides not ordered with finished ends are <strong>notched for a continuous run</strong> of light across the cabinets.</li>
  <li>The channel protrudes <strong>1/8″</strong> below the bottom of the wall cabinet.</li>
  <li>Extruded aluminum, anodized aluminum finish, frosted diffuser.</li>
  <li>Available on all wall cabinets that have a bottom shelf, <strong>except wall blind corners</strong>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Floating shelves</h3>
<ul>
  <li>For floating shelves with the <strong>Prep Floating Shelf For Lighting</strong> modification (page C2).</li>
  <li>The bottom shelf gets a <strong>centered groove</strong> for the CLC channel.</li>
  <li>The channel protrudes <strong>1/8″</strong> below the bottom of the shelf.</li>
  <li>Extruded aluminum, anodized aluminum finish.</li>
  <li>Only available on <strong>Floating Shelves (FLS)</strong> and <strong>floating vanities</strong>.</li>
  <li>The same groove is available on the <a href="/playbook/shiloh-edge-banded-shelf/">1¼″ Edge-Banded Shelf</a> as the PFSL option.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Toe kick</h3>
<ul>
  <li>For base, vanity, or utility cabinets with the <strong>Prep Base Cabinet For Toe Kick Lighting</strong> modification (page C2).</li>
  <li>The bottom shelf is grooved for the CLC channel and the sides get a <strong>pre-grooved wire chase</strong>.</li>
  <li>Base cabinet sides not ordered with finished ends are notched for a continuous run.</li>
  <li>Extruded aluminum, anodized aluminum finish, frosted diffuser.</li>
  <li>Available on all base cabinets with a <strong>recessed toe kick</strong>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Continuous pull — handleless and lit</h2>

<p>If a wall cabinet also needs to be <strong>handleless</strong>, the continuous-pull option gives you both: a profile along the bottom of the cabinet that serves as the finger pull and houses an LED diffuser.</p>

<div class="post-figure">
  <img src="/images/blog/led-prep-shiloh-eclipse/continuous-pull-led.webp" alt="Section drawing and examples of the continuous pull with LED: GWL profile 1-1/16 inch wide and 13/16 inch tall with LED diffuser, wire chase, and wall and wall square corner examples" width="1080" height="1350" loading="lazy" />
</div>

<ul>
  <li>The <strong>GWL</strong> profile measures <strong>1 1/16″</strong> wide by <strong>13/16″</strong> tall, with an LED diffuser in the channel.</li>
  <li>A <strong>wire chase</strong> runs to the profile at the wall cabinet bottom shelf.</li>
  <li>Available in <strong>wall, stacked wall, or square corner</strong> cabinets (examples shown as FWC-W and FWC-WSC).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Which one to use</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Task light on the counter</strong> → Prep Wall For Lighting (CLC under the wall cabinets).</li>
  <li><strong>Display uppers, glass doors, two-tone interiors</strong> → Internal LED prep.</li>
  <li><strong>Open shelving or floating vanities</strong> → Floating-shelf channel.</li>
  <li><strong>Night light and a floating look</strong> → Toe-kick channel.</li>
  <li><strong>Handleless wall cabinets</strong> → Continuous pull.</li>
</ul>

<p>Remember to coordinate the electrician early: the factory supplies the routes, wire chases, and channel; the LED tape, drivers, and wiring are local.</p>

